# Colocated headers and sources

A directory is one unit: the header and its implementation live **side by side**. This applies to new files and to any move or subdirectory split under `src/`, `core/`, `algorithm/`, and `testing/`.

## Do

- Put `foo.h` next to `foo.cc` or `foo.cpp` in the **same directory**.
- When splitting a module by responsibility, **move the header with its translation unit**. Includes use that path (`layer/module/unit/file.h`).
- Keep header-only companions in the directory of the module that owns them.
- In the same change, update `BUILD.gn` sources and every `#include`.
- Match the sibling extension (`.cc` or `.cpp`) already used in that subtree.

```
// GOOD
src/legacy/render/gdi/device/gdi_renderdevice.h
src/legacy/render/gdi/device/gdi_renderdevice.cpp
#include "legacy/render/gdi/device/gdi_renderdevice.h"
```

## Don’t

- **Don’t** leave public headers at the parent and move only `.cpp` into a child (headers-at-top).
- **Don’t** add an `include/` + `src/` (or `inc/` + `src/`) split for product code.
- **Don’t** leave a forwarding header at the old path after a move.
- **Don’t** drive-by relocate trees that are already colocated, or rewrite `third_party/` / `branches/`.

```
// BAD — header and body split
src/legacy/render/gdi/gdi_renderdevice.h
src/legacy/render/gdi/device/gdi_renderdevice.cpp

// BAD — parallel include tree
src/foo/include/foo/bar.h
src/foo/src/bar.cc
```

## Exceptions

- A module-root **umbrella** that only re-exports (`views.h`) may stay at that root.
- An already-locked embedder surface (`src/content/public/`) stays until its own spec moves it.
- Third-party and generated headers keep the vendor layout.

## Relation to other rules

**`.cursor/rules/style/refactoring.mdc`** (reshape by responsibility), **`.cursor/rules/style/tree-style.mdc`** (match siblings), **`docs/build/src-layout.md`** (nesting cap). Colocation wins over keeping a split include path; do not add a shim header to preserve the old path.
